WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.988
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.988 --> 00:00:05.860
 Poetry can make someone
fall in love with you.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:10.120
Poetry can make you fall
in love with yourself.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.460
I come to poetry because
of the questions.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.810
What are we doing here?

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:14.530
Why?

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.510
Who would make a
place like this?

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.100
And there's no one answer.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.180
It's to investigate.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.930
Poetry became my
activism, my own way

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.860
of processing and dealing with
the Native rights movements.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.520
It goes where words cannot go,
speaks what words cannot speak.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.565
And so then the question
is, where do I start?

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.280
I'm offering you different
kinds of approaches

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.250
to poetry or to your
innate creativity.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.750
In this class, we'll be talking
about imagery, writing, rhythm,

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:49.920
revision.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.063
And it's good for anyone.

00:00:51.063 --> 00:00:52.230
You don't have to be a poet.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.720
Everyone's paths are different.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.290
A line has to have a purpose.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.050
Otherwise, it's
like a two-by-four

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.750
going through the middle
of the room for no reason.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.640
What do you do if
you get blocked?

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.500
Go outside the predictability.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.360
Take your failed
love poem and put it

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.910
in the shape of a recipe.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:13.270
While I'm still waking up,
halfway in the dream space,

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.540
I just start writing for a
half hour without thinking.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.080
Poems come through that were
beyond the thinking mind.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.150
It will take you to other
levels of perception.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.670
Poetry can open doors.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.410
Poetry can open eyes.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:30.520
It can take our grief and turn
it to the depth, the muscle,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.480
the toughness you need
to be able to climb.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.300
I am Joy Harjo, and
this is MasterClass.

